{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have two data points: RNA-only (config_001, acc 0.485) and multimodal with PCA+ResNet50 concat (config_016, acc 0.527). The ~4% multimodal gain is promising but we cannot yet decompose it: we do not know how much of the performance comes from the image modality alone versus the combination. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the exact image-only counterpart to config_016, differing only in model_setting. This completes a clean three-way comparison (RNA-only / image-only / both) holding profile setting and image encoder constant, isolating each modality's contribution. If image-only is near 0.52, RNA adds little and we should focus on image encoder or profile improvements; if image-only is substantially lower (e.g., ~0.40), the combination is genuinely synergistic and investing in more complex multimodal configs (multiprofile, better fusion, ViT) is justified. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most important design axis (modality contribution) before spending budget on more complex configurations."
}

